"answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off on June 15th and a Phase 1 budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase through AI algorithms, to be discussed on August 5th. The project involves gathering innovative ideas by July 20th to enhance data visualization tools. The team expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th, and later welcomed Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. Following the design phase, the development phase began next month under lead developer Omar Jensen. A major milestone was reached ahead of schedule with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype, with UI enhancements planned for October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. The project is now nearing its final stages."
